  "text_sanskrit": "महर्षयः सप्त पूर्वे चत्वारो मनवस्तथा । मद्भावा मानसा जाता येषां लोक इमाः प्रजाः ॥ १०-६ ॥",
  "itrans": "maharShayaH sapta pUrve chatvAro manavastathA . madbhAvA mAnasA jAtA yeShA.n loka imAH prajAH .. 10-6 ..",
  "translation": "The seven great Rishis of the preceding Manvantara, and the four Manus born of the mind, are born of Me, as also are those who in the world are their children (6) \nV. Marichi, Atri, Angiras, Pulastya, Pulaha, Kratu and Vasishtha are the seven Rishis of old. Manvantara; the period during which a Manu rules. Svâyambhuva, Svârochisha, Raivata and Uttama are the four Manus.\nManvantara: those who are of superior wisdom, i.e., Brahma and other gods who are also divided into four classes as Brahma, Kshatriya, Vaisya and Sudra (Vide Brihad, Bhashya) Svâyambhuva and others, though commonly thought to be the creation of Brahma, are really created by Me present in Brahma as his inner guide. Brahma is only a way, as it were, for My work. \nA. The effect of knowing such glories of the Lord is declared thus:",
